<title>GERMANY: Bayer details results on per share basis.</title>
<headline>Bayer details results on per share basis.</headline>
<dateline>LEVERKUSEN, Germany 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996 (in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Dividend				     1.70    vs 1.50 marks</p>
<p>    Tax credit				   0.73    vs 0.64 marks</p>
<p>    Earnings per share (statements)	3.85    vs 3.40  marks</p>
<p>    Earnings per share (DVFA)		3.85    vs 3.40  marks</p>
<p>    Cash flow per share			8.20    vs 7.70  marks</p>
<p>    Equity per share			   28.45   vs 25.30 marks</p>
<p>    Price/ earnings ratio		    16.6     vs 11.2</p>
<p>    Price/cash flow ratio		    7.8	vs 4.9</p>
<p>    Dividend yield			     3.9	vs 5.6 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German chemicals and drugs group is Bayer AG. The group released several core figures last week after its supervisory board meeting. These numbers were released ahead of the annual news conference in Leverkusen today.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
